Rocq 9.1.1 + a conversion memo (one table per checked conversion: a pair of closure cells already found
convertible, or not, at a pair of lifts, is answered from the table), backported from rocq-prover/rocq#22309
(kernel/cClosure.ml: a stable cell identity [fid], 0 for every cell built, kept by the in-place [update]; the
ConvCache module; kernel/conversion.ml: the lookup in [ccnv], on for checked conversion [gen_conv], off for
unification [generic_conv]).  ROCQ_CONV_CACHE=0 turns it off.  Apply with: git apply -p1 (or patch -p1) in a V9.1.1 tree.
See Rocq-C-solution.md F46 and D28.
